# Overrides semgrep's built-in ignore list.
#
# The default list excludes `tests/` and `test/`, which means security rules
# silently skip every test file in the repository. That is the wrong default
# twice over: test code runs in CI with real credentials often enough to matter,
# and — for this repository specifically — the guardrail fixtures live under
# tests/, so the default would have made the secret-scanning fixture invisible
# and the rule would have looked healthy while never being exercised.
#
# This file is deliberately short. Everything not listed here gets scanned.

# Dependencies and build output: not our code, and scanning it produces noise
# nobody can act on.
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.terraform/
.tools/

# Version control internals.
.git/

